        <body>
            <div>
                <head>Comments</head>
                <p xml:id="CH8x3403-start">
                    <seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-18T22:46:44.769+09:00">粟 does not refer to millet here but to all kinds of grain in general with regard to its expected yield.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-18T22:47:52.812+09:00">輒 means "immediately" in administrative texts like this.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-18T22:49:27.935+09:00">頃數 forms the core of the nominal phrase that is the object of the verb 言.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-18T23:02:45.389+09:00">早 is a misspelling of 旱.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-18T23:19:39.763+09:00">Both 𧈸 (zhong) and 䖵 (kun) are umbrella terms for flying and crawling creatures that harm the crop.</seg>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
